# The Analyst Agent

A **brain** is a system prompt, a model, and a set of tools, run as a loop on the
**server**. Native Elixir on the BEAM drives it: call the model, run the tool it
asks for, feed the result back, repeat. The browser never sees a key.

agent :analyst do
  model "minimax/minimax-m3"

  system """
  You draft the first outreach email to a ranked lead. One angle per lead, picked
  from its shape. Two sentences, one question. Name the company. Stop when every top
  lead has a draft.
  """

  tools [AnalystTools.top_leads(), AnalystTools.draft()]
end

`system` is the policy; `tools` is the capability surface. A **tool is just a server
function** — no DSL, the module is the contract.

defmodule AnalystTools do
  def top_leads(limit \\ 3) do
    Pipeline.ranked() |> Enum.filter(&(&1.status == :scored)) |> Enum.take(limit)
  end

  def draft(%Lead{name: name} = lead), do: %Draft{lead: lead, subject: subject_for(name)}
end

**Memory is typed data, not a transcript blob** — a struct the loop can query, so the
trace is auditable on the [[The Code Graph]]:

defmodule Draft do
  defstruct lead: nil, subject: "", body: "", angle: :value
end

It runs on the server because it needs the model key and shared state, and must
survive a refresh. Each draft becomes a `%Task{}` on the [[Plan]] board. Next:
[[Coder]].
